There is a switch labeled S3 on the back of the machine.  (On some early
VS3100s, there isn't a cutout on the case and you have to go inside the
machine to get to it.)  If you flip this switch (up, I think), the
serial port with the printer icon becomes the console port.

The terminal should be set to 9600-8-N-1.

One word of caution:  If you are running VMS, leave a keyboard connected
to the VS3100.  You will still use the keyboard on the terminal and not
the one on the VS3100.

If a keyboard is not connected, VMS wants a VAXserver license.  If the
keyboard is connected, VMS uses a VAXstation license.

Good luck!

