Ron wrote:
> 
> Hi Folks:

> Also, does anyone know of a 'generic' monitor that will work with the
> 3100 or am I stuck?  Are the sync signals available from the DB-15 on
> the back of the machine?  Anyone know where I can get a monitor that
> will work with this machine (and won't cost me an arm and a leg to
> ship)?

It depends on the video board you have.

If you don't have a video board, the graphics are monochrome, 1024x864,
60Hz.

With the GPX video board, the graphics are color, sync on green,
1024x864, 60Hz.

With the SPX video board, the graphics are color, sync on green,
1280x1024, 66Hz.  (The SPX can also be switched to the same
resolution/frequency as the GPX.)

Any terminal which meets these specs should work.  The sync on green is
usually the problem.

If it comes down to it, I have a VR260 (1024x864 mono) or VR290
(1024x864 color) that I could sell you.  (Don't hold me to it, but I
think the shipping is about $40.)

If the monitor that died is a VR260, the odds are that the video
deflection board failed.  If you are comfortable with going inside the
monitor, you can save on shipping by just having this board shipped to
you.  You will probably find that the board will cost as much as the
whole monitor since this is almost always the part that fails.

