There is a switch, S3, that when placed in its upward position enables
the serial port as console.  On some 3100s you have to remove the cover
to get to the switch, others have it accessible.  Use the port with the
printer icon.  Comm settings are 9600, 8 bits, no parity.

>Also, does anyone know of a 'generic' monitor that will work with the
>3100 or am I stuck?  Are the sync signals available from the DB-15 on
>the back of the machine?  Anyone know where I can get a monitor that
>will work with this machine (and won't cost me an arm and a leg to
>ship)?

Just about any multi-synch monitor that supports a synch-on-green video
input will work.  It is easier if it also has RGB inputs.  I have a
Viewsonic PS90 to use with my 3100-M76.  There are other manufacturers
whose monitors will do synch-on-green as well.

