The question on how to access the serial console comes up at least once a
month on the comp.os.vms newsgroup.  The question about the monitor
replacement comes up about twice a year and is not currently in the FAQ.

Specifically the console port information is at:

http://www.openvms.digital.com/wizard/openvms_faq.html#VAX9

Which serial port is the console on the MicroVAX 3100?

Just to keep life interesting, the MicroVAX 3100 has some "interesting"
console ports behaviours based on the setting of the BREAK enable switch.
When the console is not enabled to respond to BREAK, MMJ-1 is the console
port. MMJ-3 will (confusingly) output the results of the selftest in
parallel with MMJ-1. When the console is enabled to respond to BREAK, MMJ-3
becomes the console port, and MMJ-1 will (confusingly) output the results of
selftest in parallel with MMJ-3.


The wiring diagram for the serial port is given at:

http://www.openvms.digital.com/wizard/openvms_faq.html#MISC1

