The 4000-300 does not have any grant cards in it at all. Strangely enough, this
does not prevent it from seeing the half-height (2-high) TKQ70 controller and
tape drive. I have been told it does not need them (hardware reason unknown by
informant who is a software engineer).

I did try the RXV21+RX02 on the microvax 3900 which is a KA655 ("microvax III").
This machine does require grant cards in the lower four slots of each Qbus bay.
I get the same result as with the VAX 4000-300, which I have never seen grant
cards used in, and which has been working well without them.

On both machines, the "show qbus" command divulges the existance of the RXV21.
On both systems, the "show device" command obfuscates the existance of the card
in the bus.

I have grokked after this all night, standing near the 3900, typing into the
VT240 and meditating upon the system managers' manual, and the sysgen
autoconfigure commands and device names, have possibly been enlightened::

The pdp11/23 uses an RXV21 with the RX02, as that is where the RXV21 and RX02
came from.
The pdp11 Qbus hardware manuals always list the RXV21controller.
The aforementioned VMS manual calls for an RV211controller for the RX02,
Therefore the VAX 3900 and 4000-300 Qbus machines desire an RV211 controller.

Have I answered my own question, and if so, anyone know where I can get an RV211
for cheep?

thank you all very much!
Pat Jankowiak
