> The Q-Bus in the VAX 4000 model 300 was 22 bits. As shipped, the system
> generally had bus grant continuity cards in place. That is, each slot would
> have had a grant card.

Q-bus are always 22-bit address. However, unlike the Unibus, the Q-bus
only needed bus grants up to the last card, not the end of the bus.

> Are all the grant cards in place, or did the former owner remove one option
> and neglect to replace the grant card.
> 
> The cards are small, 2 inch square items, with nothing on them but a circuit
> etch.

That's the unibus bus grant continuity card you're talking about. Don't
put
one of them in a q-bus. Q-bus grant cards are full size.

If I'm wrong, I sure hope someone will correct me. I'm a little weak on
q-bus, being mostly a Unibus guy myself...

