Who said it goes to the needing by putting it up on eBay? If anything,
it is even
less likely to happen in that case, since the most needing seldom have
money
enough to pay high prices. It often cost enough just to keep these
machines running.

I very much dislike eBay myself. Even though I can afford some stuff, I
think it
bodes ill for the future when people start making profits on people who
in
my view just are trying to do a good thing out of pure idealism. It's
not
like they ever expect this to be a profit. I do agree that it's better
that
items go on aBay instead of being thrown away. But get realistic here.
These items were previously thrown away, since they don't hold any
actual
value. Now smoe are realising that crazyheads who like to get old
hardware
running might need this information, and thus they now (sometimes) want
to make a profit from you. It's not like they have put any money on the
line
themself. Most of these items are put up by people who just happened to
grab
a copy of something from the company when things were thrown out. Or
perhaps
they were given a copy by DEC for promotion, or whatever.

