I've just been informed by the legal folks at Amazon.com that
the CD collections of PDP-11 freeware will no longer be available
through their web site.  They require that I have
explicit permission from each and every author on the CD,
something that isn't particularly practical when we're talking
about tens of thousands of authors (all of whom did sign at least
the DECUS forms at the time, but DECUS no longer has paperwork
from that long ago) and software up to 30 years old.  There was
no specific complaint to Amazon; they're just enforcing a newly-
written policy.

The CD's will still be available direct from me, and of course
the freeware collections will continue to be available over the
web and by anonymous FTP.  In the next few days I will try to make
all the virtual disk images easily accessible, as this is
far and away the easiest way to access the collections en masse.
Watch

  http://www.trailing-edge.com/www/freeware.html

for massive updates and HTML-ization of the PDP-11 Freeware FAQ.

Sorry for the legal hassles; I certainly understand the CYA
action by Amazon.com, though I would have preferred that they
had instead understood the history of the PDP-11 community
sharing software instead.

