Hi!

I have a problem with the tabs parameter in stty on dunix.

I need to transfer data to and from a PC running WinLink terminal
software. This software only supports X-modem protocol over telnet.

The actual transfer runs OK from the PC to the dunix box, but the other
way xmodem gives CRC errors.

I've found out that the cause seems to be that stty converts all
tabulator characters to spaces, and the tabs parameters is doing exactly
that according to the man pages, and it's enabled per default with the
terminal used (vt220).
Also according to the manual, the tabs parameter is a Compaq special
parameter, and I've checked on other unices (AIX & HP), and here the
tabs is not present per default..... and transfers to a AIX box is
tested and is working..... som I'm pretty sure it's the stty tabs
causing the problems.


I then tried to do a stty -tabs to disable tabs, but this somehow gets
reset in the process of transferring the files, so I can't use this.

I then wanted to disable it from /etc/termcap, but I don't know what
termcap parameter I should use to disable tabs.

On Linux I found this :

# The tab is destructive on the Ozzie; make sure to 'stty -tabs'.
ozzie|osborne|osborne1|osborne 1:\
        :ms:ul:xt:\
        :co#104:li#24:\
        :al=\EE:bl=^G:ce=\ET:cl=^Z:cm=\E=%+ %+ :cr=^M:dc=\EW:\
        :dl=\ER:do=^J:ei=:ic=\EQ:im=:kd=^J:kl=^H:kr=^L:ku=^K:\
        :le=^H:nd=^L:se=\E(:sf=^J:so=\E):ue=\Em:up=^K:us=\El:


...but using some of this on a dunix box doesn't seem to have any
effect.


Anyone with an idea about how to permanently disable tabs ?



l8r/Jspr



