> the problem with electronic storage is, of course,
> that media and formats change constantly, so the corpus of knowledge will
> need constant conversion.  And naturally that will never happen, so as
> we move away from paper and libraries, every new generation of electronic
> storage, every new OS, etc, will result in another chunk of human history
