'Appen not. As new generations evolve, so the problems of decyphering
old formats becomes trivial. The problem lies not in the data format but
in the hardware format the data is on. So long as the data is on the net
it is available as long as the hardware it exists on is running, and
that hardware is, hopefully, a constantly evolving set. 

It is difficult nowadays to get data off of 8" disks, and the last time
I tried to get anything off of a 5 1/4" disk it only worked once before
the accumulation af dust in the seldom-used drive buggered the disk. 

Hardware formats are the problem, not software ones. 

