PatJ wrote:
> 
> Here we go again.. I seem to get ahold of the wierdest hardwares..
> 
> I've got a microvax 4000-300 and an RX02 floppy. I would like to read 8" disks
> with the VAX using the 'exchange' utility. I have as a controller for the RX02,
> the RXV21 LSI11 RX02 Controller. I plugged this into the qbus of the 4000-300
> and aside from an occasional grunt, the vax ignores it.
> Additionally,
> $ autoconfig all
> produces an interminable wait, and no end or result.

The CSR and/or vector set on the RXV21 may not be what is expected
for the autoconfigure rules.  It should have a CSR of 777170 and
a vector of 264.

You can find the address and CSR jumper settings for the RXV21
at

 
http://metalab.unc.edu/pub/academic/computer-science/history/pdp-11/hardware/

in the file 'rxv21.info'.

> Will the RXV21 not work in the MicroVAX

It certainly does work in a Microvax II or "III" (i.e. KA650 or
KA655)...

>, or is it contending with the DSSI
> controller or something? I realize the RXV21 is a pdp card. Qbus is not Qbus?

It may be that the Q-bus adapter on the 4000-300 simply doesn't
support the RXV21 for some reason.  I don't think it's because the
RXV21 only supports 18-bit addressing, because the other Q-bus
Microvaxes use a driver that knows how to work around this particular
limitation.  Can you do a "SHOW QBUS" from
the ">>>" prompt and at least confirm the CSR?

