Basically these terminals are multi-page, multi-session capable.  The real
information you will need is how to make the proper cables to connect them
to your box.  There is a wiring diagram which is floating around which
will give you the proper connections so that you can use standard (6
conductor) phone cord to build a line (this is what I did, total cost was
about $7 by the time I bought a 25foot cord and 9DB solder connector at
the local Radio Shack).

Other than that what you need to know is that these terminals operate in
VT52/100/102/220 modes with regard to control sequences, and can be
configured in the setup screens for various features.

Over all they are extremely nice terminals, and the small footprint
combined with the multi-session capablity make them ideal for managing
headless systems and debugging network setups.
 

