Here is some clarification straight from the horse's mouth, as it were..

       C came into being in the years 1969-1973, in parallel with the early
       development of the Unix operating system; the most creative period
       occurred during 1972. Another spate of changes peaked between 1977
       and 1979, when portability of the Unix system was being demonstrated.
       In the middle of this second period, the first widely available
       description of the language appeared: The C Programming Language,
       often called the `white book' or `K&R' [Kernighan 78]. 
               From: "The Development of the C Language", Dennis M. Ritchie

Much more historical info is available on his HomePage and I would guess
his having been there :-) vouches for its accuracy.

bill 

