The History Center is indeed a real resource and is altogether neat.
It suffers in terms of general-public attendance because it
it does take a bit of hassle to visit and to get in, and is not staffed
as a full-time public museum--at least according to their WWW
page it's either Wednesday afternoons or by appointment.
Partly this is because of the Moffett Field location, partly
because looking at (or even playing with) old computers draws
only a limited--albeit very fascinated--clientele.  I don't
know the full story of the merger/acquision/split of the Computer
Museum in Boston with the Boston Science Museum, but ultimately
it must have had to do with the tension between having a place
to entertain and excite families and middle-school classes of
kids, versus displaying a historical collection.

	Dennis



