No, actually MS is arguing that, as a work of art, Windows is entitled
to remain whole and uncut, which was the gist of the Python vs ABC suit.
ABC wanted to run edited Python skits but the copyright holder argued
successfully that the skit should remain unedited as a work of art.  It
has nothing to do with Netscape.

It's a clever comparison.  Snide remarks about art aside, MS does have a
point, they are entitled to ship a "work of art" whole and complete,
without the government compelling them to remove or add certain items.

What if you are an author and your publisher unilaterally decides to
remove half the chapters you wrote and add in chapters from another
author, but only puts your name on the book?
    Jack Peacock




