Bob,

Would advise against that. A switch mode psu is not inductive, typically having
a really weird power factor, so you could end up with unpredictable voltages at
the other side of the cap which will vary with load.

Best to buy a solid state phase convertor (See industrial machinery vendors) or
rewire the input circuitry for single phase, though you may have to upgrade the
capacitors and bridge rectifier if you are going from 6 diode bridge to 4. Maybe
these machines have a battery backup option ?. If so, you could just generate
the required DC and feed appropriately.

This sort of thing is _not_ for the faint hearted...

Rgrds, Chris

 

