:we've got a DECcluster consisting of two Alpha 4100's running openVMS
:7.2. We have been experiencing problems while trying to log on to the
:console (which is running CDE). Basically, one out of two times the
:whole system freezes and needs to be reset on the front panel. This
:happens on both machines.
:
:Has anybody ever had similar problems, and if so, what was the cause?

  Yep.  Usually missing ECOs or system-tuning problems.  But I don't 
  know enough about this environment to begin to guess -- version 
  information for DECwindows and OpenVMS at a minimum, as well as the
  particular graphics controller in use and the names of any of the
  ECO(s) presently installed, as well as the specific AlphaServer 4100 
  series model.  

  I'd also clean the cruft out of MODPARAMS.DAT and then run a pass of 
  AUTOGEN with FEEDBACK, and reboot.

:As we don't need CDE on the console anyway, we want to disable it and
:get the text-based login prompt back. Unfortunately, nobody in our
:company knows how, and apparently does not want to ask 
:DE^Higita^H^H^H^H^H^HCompaq for info.
:
:Does anybody here know how to do this?

  Set the system parameter WINDOW_SYSTEM to 0 in OpenVMS and also set the 
  console enviroment variable to serial, and set up a serial console using
  a traditional VT-style terminal, PC emulator, or similar...

  Note that the graphics console on this and on most other OpenVMS systems
  is exceedingly stupid when DECwindows or some other controlling software
  is not running, though Alpha graphics console systems tend to be not quite 
  as stupid as some of the VAX graphics monitors.  (eg: VT52-like vs "glass 
  TTY".)  The graphics displays on these systems are far more primitive than
  a traditional serial terminal -- when no controlling software is running,
  that is...

