Frans Trip (tripf@vertis.nl) wrote:
: No graphics on install !!!
: Do i need to config the graphics card ?      (S3 by dec)
: 
: If yes,    how ????

Hi,

To install Tru64, you must be running the SRM console, so you should
see a '>>>' prompt.  It should recognize the graphics card.  Use the
'>>> show conf' to show all the adapters in your system.  If your
graphics card is not listed by the console, T64 will not use it for the
install.  If it does not see the card, I recommend upgrading your
firmware to the newest level appropriate for your release of T64.

Another thing to check: if '>>> show console' says 'serial',
do '>>> set console graphics' and '>>> init' and try again.

If you have a valid T64 anywhere on the system, try booting
genvmunix (>>> boot -fi genvmunix) and running 'doconfig'
to rebuild the kernel.  Please read the systemd admin manual
for all the steps you need for rebuilding the kernel.

Good luck!

