It looks like this is a DECstation 3100, a MIPS machine.  As a result your
best bet will probably be NetBSD, or OpenBSD.  FreeBSD doesn't support MIPS,
and I'm not sure of the status of Linux on these boxes.  You can get Y2k
patches for Ultrix, I believe there specific to V4.5 though, and they cost
money.

If you've got apps that require Ultrix, upgrading the version of Ultrix is
your best bet.  Otherwise I'd say go with either NetBSD or OpenBSD.

