    Yes, IIRC the 3100 still has battery backed PROM settings/time. If you
disconnect the battery for a while (5 minutes say?). Then when you boot
Ultrix won't know what time/date it is, and *should* boot correctly,
assuming that was the problem.
    I can't speak for FreeBSD, but NetBSD has a bootable kernel disk image
with an mfs file system in it that you can dd onto your HD with a helper
machine if you want to scrap Ultrix. I would guess that FreeBSD has
something similar. From there you'll need something with the distribution
sets on it. NetBSD can read an ISO9660 CD if you have a CD reader, or you
can also NFS mount it over the net or FTP it onto another disk/machine/tape
(tape will be SLOW!) </shameless NetBSD plug>

