Brian,

There two obstacles to trying this out: 1) With the latest AS400 firmware, you
can't use ARC console to reflash the bios, so you can't get srm into the machine
using 'approved' procedures. 2) There may be not enough space to load both SRM
and ARC in XL series machines, whereas the AS400 probably has larger flash
devices.

The bios update actually contains 3 images: The update utility and the two
bios's. If there was some way of splitting the image into it's components, you
could maybe run the update utility standalone and choose which bios image to
load by naming the files appropriately.

All this requires more information, such as: 

1) Where all the 3 components start and end in the bios update file so it can be
split.

2) Details of how the bios update works, internals, memory space used etc, or
where to find such info.

3) If there are any really old AS400 bios versions that do allow update from ARC
console + where can these be found. Once an SRM image is loaded, you could then
bootstrap up to the latest version.

Wouldn't be surprised if someone within Dec already did this years ago. How
about a few clues ?. Could be quite usefull to those stuck with Alpha hardware
and no supported OS to run on it...

Rgrds, Chris


Brian wrote:

If you can get this to work, I'd really like to hear about it!  I've got a
XL 300 which would make a nice vms box....

Brian



