You should not need to do so. Just install OpenVMS (from what? Do you
have a SCSI CD-ROM or a TZ50 or some other tape?). The command (to
stand-alone BACKUP):

$ BACKUP/IMAGE ddcu: ddcu:/INIT

...should do just fine, so long as the low-level format of the disk is
intact. DOS formatting is meaningless to OpenVMS.

If you're installing NetBSD or OpenBSD, the software install should
provide some help in this area.

