If you use a terminal server (not the Ds100 or DS200) which supports telnet,
then that
will work.
A VAX may be used as a terminal server, in the sense that you can telnet
from the
VAX to the linux box using ethernet.

From the VAX to the linux box via a serial port is also possible, on the vax
use SET HOST/DTE.
Assuming that /dev/cua0 or whatever is correctly set up on unix.

Samba should work as terminal emulator and if all you need is a character
interface, try kermit.

