Bill Tedeski wrote:
> 
> can a vaxstation 4000 vlc be booted from a vt200 type console?
> if so how do I set it up and what do I need to use a PC emulator
> as the VT200.


On the side of the VLC (near the halt button) is a switch labeled S3. 
Flip it up.

On the back of the VLC is a MMJ socket with a printer icon next to it. 
With S3 up, this is the console port.

Use an MMJ cable with an appropriate adapter for your terminal (if
needed) and you are all set.

Good luck!

