I suggested at the time of the debacle that one reason for the drop in
Alpha/NT system sales might have been the imminent prospect of W2K.  In
fact, it wouldn't surprise me if *all* NT sales were in least somewhat
depressed last year compared to normal projections.

W2K is a major step from NT4, and it would not be unreasonable for a lot of
prospective customers to have adopted a 'wait and see' attitude - to see if
W2K was real, was real on Alpha too, or was sufficiently disappointing to
consider sticking with NT4 or moving to a different platform entirely.
Multiply this by (obviously justifiable, in hindsight) concerns about
Compaq's commitment, factor in Alan's performance observations, and a big
Alpha/NT sales dip in 1999 seems almost inevitable.

Certainly not my area of expertise, but it seems at least possible.

- bill

