OK, I give up.  Spent half this weekend websearching for oscillators
compatible with my AS200 4/166; I want to upgrade it to 233MHz.  I
already have the faster rated CPU installed and running fine.

The oscillator has the following on it:

     RFM HC1282
      333 MHZ
      9606A

It appears to be a 14-pin DIP size with pins 1,7,8,14 being discrete
connections, pins 2,6,9,13 grounded to the case, and no pins for the 
remaining positions.

My AS200 manuals both indicate that the clock source on the AS200 is
the oscillator insteadof a PLL; this is different from some of the 
various OEM ALpha boards that used Triquint clock chips, apparently.

I cannot locate a manufacturer, nor any equivalent to this part, nor
for the 466MHz unit apparently needed to run at 233MHz.  I called Allied
Electronics, JDR, and Digikey, all to no avail.

Obviously I only need one though if they are not too expensive I'd buy
one or two extras (for future upgrades on another couple stations I 
might get my hands on).  Any info on where to get these, or pointers
to a manufacturer would be greatly appreciated.


Rich Jordan
rjordan@mcs.net
still oozing along at 166MHz...




