Most of the major brand stuff wasn't bad.

OTOH, I have a client who has 3 wkstns (based on 1995-vintage
ASUS 486 boards with AWARD BIOS) that if you try to set any
date >12/31/1999, the next time you reboot or power cycle, 
it sets the date to the year 2054.

How thoughtful of the BIOS manufacturer to include such
forward-thinking year settings... which are totally
useless.

Unlike what you may read in the National Enquirer or
USA today, the "Y2K bug" was real, and would have been
even more real to you today if the world hadn't spent 
nearly half a trillion dollars addressing it.



