> is HSZ70 a controller which supports hot-swapping ?

Yes.

> Could I do a hot-swapping operation on a classic KZPXX SCSI controller.
> I've got a 2 nodes cluster with LSM & ASE, 1 shared SCSI bus.
> On the shared bus I've got 2 disks in mirroring. Can I hot-swap one
> of the mirrored disk even if I have no HSZ controller ?

Yes.

The main issue is where the termination is located, and in what box the
disks are located.
As long as you don't break termination when you remove or add disks, and
the controller can handle it (most, if not all DEC controlloers do),
there's no problem.

Usually, the disks will be located in some StorageWorks BA box, and all
of this will not be an issue because those boxes are built to support
hot swap.

We never take our machines down unless we have to do a complete
re-configuration or something like that.
That's also the beauty of it... when you need more diskspace you plug in
a couple of new disks, do a scu scan, make some device files, put some
disklabel on and then do a addvol to some AdvFS domain to dynamically
extend its size; all while in production.

Ofcourse it's best to do this while not in production and with the
machine turned off, just to minimize the risk of human error... but
sometimes this is not possible.



