Imagine - if circa. 2GB StorageWorks disk drives could be combined in a
StorageWorks array with Castlewood Orb Drives (2 GB removable cartridge
disk drives).

Wanna take "backups" COMPLETELY off of OpenVMS?

Mirror the non-removable disks to the removable disks. Then, quiesce (or
shutdown) your system or application, split the Orb disks (removeable
disks) out of the mirror-sets, start your system/app. back up, change
the removable media, and trickle the removeable drives back into their
mirror-sets. Do this everyday, and your "backup" window is as small as
the time it takes to split the mirror-sets (can be automated in some
cases). The mirror copies on the HSx's will pose little or no detriment
to the running systems.

