You need to think about what that really means.

Here's the traceback from a VMS system (21064A, DEC C V6.0-001 on 
OpenVMS Alpha V7.2-1, but these facts are not crucial here).

%SYSTEM-F-HPARITH, high performance arithmetic trap, Imask=00000000, Fmask=00000
001, summary=08, PC=00000000000200C4, PS=0000001B
-SYSTEM-F-FLTOVF, arithmetic trap, floating overflow at PC=00000000000200C4, PS=
0000001B
%TRACE-F-TRACEBACK, symbolic stack dump follows
  image    module    routine             line      rel PC           abs PC
 TEST  TEST  main                           6 00000000000000C4 00000000000200C4
 TEST  TEST  __main                         0 0000000000000068 0000000000020068
                                            0 FFFFFFFF82A913D4 FFFFFFFF82A913D4

It's pretty obvious that you're getting overflow.  (I REALLY like the 
fact that /DEBUG=(TRACEBACK,NOSYMBOLS) is the default on VMS.)  Yes, 
some other systems don't notice the overflow, `run fine' and produce 
garbage.  I would rather have a program crash than run wrongly.




