This whole issue seems to have a simple solution.  The institution and the
instructor cannot use the licenses to teach students, this is a
commercial/educational use of the license.  If the license is issued to the
student, then the student can use the license as part of his studies as long as
he doesn't sell his class projects.

When I was in school (seems that such a thing occured in the dim (real dim)
past) the students had to purchase their books, paper, pencils, pens, and other
course material.  It's real simple.  Have the purchase of the license, or the
free obtaining of the license, a required step in getting ready for courses that
have such need.  I'm sure the institution can have the appropriate
materials/information available for getting the various licenses.  Info on
joining DECUS and getting the HOBBY license wouldn't be so hard to do.  The
school could provide the media, I'm sure they would have that.  If the product
is already loaded, that should be Ok.

