Hi folks,

	Please excuse what may be a very stupid question ... I like to think of
myself as a software guy, not a hardware guy ;-)

	I am trying to get a new AlphaPC 164 board with the 433MHz 21164
processor going.  I have tried hooking it up to a standard ATX PC power
supply and case that I know works (indeed I'm typing this message on the
machine that is normally in that case).  In summary I can't even get the
CPU fan to spin, let alone get anything else happening.  I'm a bit
confused how the whole thing is supposed to work because there doesn't
seem to be anywhere to put the standard connection to the power switch. 
There is a jumper for HALT but the manual says that isn't usable under
NT so I assume you're not supposed to use that (besides, connecting that
to the power switch doesn't do anything).  I remember when assembling
the PC that is normally in there that it too was rather fussy about
connections and wouldn't power up either unless everything was hooked up
right.  In any case, how are you supposed to turn the machine on if it
isn't connected to the power switch?

	Just to try it out I hooked up the CPU fan to one of the connectors on
my Pentium III board and noticed that it didn't spin there either
although it looks like the 12V/GND signal are around the other way
compared to the Alpha board...  I notice the manual says the system will
reset if the fan sense signal isn't okay, which I take to mean the
system will act dead if this signal doesn't work at all (possibly the
problem?).

	Can someone please enlighten me as to how this is supposed to work?


Thanks.



P.S.  Please followup to the newsgroup since the machine mentioned in
the Reply-To header my still be down (Y2K precaution....)

--
James Macnicol



