I think you will find each FAB generation is quite a step from the preceding
one.  I am under the impression that one of the big things that gets upgraded
is cleanliness of the environment (number of dust particles per unit volume of
air).  My understanding about vibration isolation is that the main need is in
just a limited area of the FAB.  If I recall correctly from a visit to the
(then) DEC FAB a few years before the current one was opened was that the main
building was built around the critical area but isolated from it.  The had
separate foundations and I suspect the foundation of the critical area was
constructed differently.

But in general it is still treated as a black art.  Once you get a process
working you don't change ANYTHING.

Bob

